Time Management

As a Texas Tech K-12 student, you will need to develop personal time management plans to maintain steady progress toward course completion. By setting aside specific hours each day for your coursework, setting your own deadlines, and staying in contact with your teachers via course messaging, you will create an environment that enhances your learning experience. Ask your parents and tutors to teach and guide you regarding time management and study skills, including:

Step 1: keeping an academic calendar to be aware of upcoming assignments and exams and complete them in a timely manner;

Step 2: reading and following instructions on the assignments;

Step 3: maintaining contact with your teachers; and

Step 4: maintaining satisfactory progress in all courses.

Carefully read all course materials before beginning coursework, particularly each course syllabus. The course syllabus will contain information and expectations to assist you in obtaining academic success.

You will spend approximately 90-100 hours per course enrollment. Because Texas Tech K-12 courses are asynchronous, the amount of actual time you spend on a course will depend on your previous knowledge and skills in the course content area.

After you have successfully enrolled in one or more courses, you should:

Step 1: log in to the Texas Tech K-12 Portal within the first two days of enrolling;

Step 2: read and print the course syllabus;

Step 3: become familiar with the Canvas Learning Management System;

Step 4: read all material titled Introduction and Course Navigation;

Step 5: follow sections of the course content in order;

Step 6: work in courses on a regular basis by participating:

Step 7: in discussion boards and forums;

Step 8: in graded instructional items, quizzes, and assignments; and

Step 9: through follow-up on feedback posted to assignment submissions.

